# Battle records the running server writes. `battleapi.DefaultBattleDir` and
# `simrun.DefaultBattleDir` are both `logs/battles`, relative to the process's
# working directory, so any test or server started in this directory leaves one
# here. These are runtime output and reproducible output: a record is worth
# keeping when a bug needs one, and it belongs in a bug report or /tmp, not in
# the tree where the next `git add -A` commits it as source.
logs/

# `go build` output from the module root (`go build ./cmd/simrun` writes here).
/simrun

# `go test -c` output. The root .gitignore already covers *.test; repeated here
# because this file is the one a reader of services/simulation/ will find.
/*.test